// Genuinely ambiguous utterances (13 cases). QUARANTINED FROM THE HEADLINE.
//
// Every case here carries an `acceptable` set: outcomes two competent people
// would disagree about. They are scored into their own bucket and are EXCLUDED
// from routing precision, routing recall and the false-positive/negative counts.
//
// The reason is anti-gaming, and it is worth stating plainly: if ambiguous cases
// counted toward the headline, the cheapest way to raise precision would be to
// relabel the awkward ones. Quarantining them means a threshold can only be met
// by changing behaviour. Their agreement rate is still reported — a collapse
// here is a real signal — it just cannot move the number that gates Phase 2.
//
// Moving a case INTO this file after seeing a score is forbidden. The corpus
// review in the manual procedure happens before any run for exactly that reason.

